From: Beryl 7 integration <noreply@github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mt7996: always build host TXWI on MT7990

The MT7990 path can mishandle Ethernet-encapsulated TX frames when TXWI
is left for firmware construction. Force the host to populate TXWI on
MT7990 while retaining the upstream behavior for other MT799x devices.

This is deliberately scoped to MT7990; do not change TX descriptor
handling for MT7992/MT7996 devices.

--- a/mt7996/mac.c
+++ b/mt7996/mac.c
@@ -1143,6 +1143,6 @@ int mt7996_tx_prepare_skb(struct mt76_dev *mdev, void *txwi_ptr,
 
 	/* mt76_tx_status_skb_add() clears info->control.flags */
-	host_txd = !is_8023 ||
+	host_txd = is_mt7990(&dev->mt76) || !is_8023 ||
 		   (info->control.flags & (IEEE80211_TX_CTRL_STREAM_CLASSIFIED |
 					   IEEE80211_TX_CTRL_EXPLICIT_UP));
 
